course: dictionary
lesson: 8426
title: Rye, a grain and a bread
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Rye is a cereal grass that farmers grow for its grain, the small seeds that are ground into flour. Like wheat, oats and barley, it is a cereal, and it grows well in cold places where the soil is poor.
explain: Look at the words around rye to find its meaning. «Roots hold a plant in the ground and take in water and minerals» tells you this lesson is about plants, so rye means the plant here. «Rye bread» is a kind of bread, and dark and heavy tell you what sort it is.
explain: Rye has more than one meaning. A field of rye is a field of grass plants. In the US and Canada, rye can mean a strong drink. Rye with a capital R is also a town in East Sussex. Always check the clues before you choose a meaning.
fact: Rye is a cereal grass, and its grain is used for flour, bread and animal food.
fact: Rye bread is a dark, heavy bread made with rye flour.
fact: «Khlib» means bread, often dark rye, and grannies frown on dropping or throwing it because it is respected.
fact: One rye plant's roots, laid end to end, were measured at over 600 kilometres long.
fact: Rye is also the name of an old town in East Sussex, England, and in the US and Canada, rye can mean rye whiskey, a strong alcoholic drink.
exercise: In a field of rye, what is rye? | *A cereal grass grown on farms | A type of stone used for paths | A bird that lives near water | A tall tree that drops its leaves
exercise: Mum buys dark, heavy rye bread from the bakery. What is rye bread made with? | Sugar and cocoa | Oats only | *Rye flour | Cheese and butter
exercise: Which name in this lesson is a town in East Sussex? | *Rye | Ryegrass | Roots | Khlib
test: Why do farmers grow rye in cold places with poor soil? | To feed fish in ponds | *Because rye grows well in cold places with poor soil | Because rye only grows in hot deserts | To make paper for books
test: «Roots are covered with tiny root hairs.» What do the root hairs help a rye plant do? | Turn grain into flour | *Soak up water and minerals | Grow bright flowers | Fly up towards the sun
exam: «The rye in the field swayed gently in the wind.» What does rye mean here? | A town in Sussex | *A cereal grass grown for its grain | A strong drink | A loaf of dark bread
